lmrs-container (0.1.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the root cause of vLLM never serving: the image declared VOLUME for
    /var/lmrs/hf-cache while the runner bind-mounted only the parent /var/lmrs,
    so docker shadowed the cache with a fresh anonymous volume on every start
    and vLLM silently re-downloaded the model instead of loading it from disk.
    The VOLUME declarations are removed and the runner bind-mounts hf-cache and
    lmcache explicitly, which also overrides the declaration in older images.
  * An admitted chat request whose runtime call fails is now reported as a
    failed command with the runtime reason code instead of a success.
  * The estimate command accepts the JSON shapes a remote client sends.

 -- Vasiliy Zdanovskiy <vasilyvz@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:40:00 +0300
